Changed: Select the points of the IBTK::LEInteractor::interpolate() and spread() overloads that take IBTK::LIndexSetData by one cell of the level per point, computed from the domain origin after the position is wrapped into each periodic direction, and remove their periodic shift argument. Make IBTK::LEInteractor::buildLocalIndices() for index data public; it takes the positions and returns the cells and in-cell fractions of the selected points. IBTK::LIndexSetData::cacheLocalIndices() takes the grid geometry and the refinement ratio of the level instead of the periodic shift, and stops with an error unless the physical domain is a single rectangular box. Add IBTK::wrap_into_periodic_interval() and the IBTK::LIndexSetData functions getPeriodicOffsets(), getDomainXLower(), getDomainXUpper(), getLevelDx(), getLevelDomainBox(), and getLevelPeriodicShift(). Add the optional argument X_data_ghost_node_update to IBTK::LDataManager::interp(), which determines whether interp() updates the ghost positions. interp() leaves the ghost values of its output invalid.
<br>
(Boyce Griffith, 2026/11/02)
